 www.netroadshow.com\n\nDeal context:\nNational Securities Clearing Corp (N
 SCCLF) is launching a three-tranche USD benchmark senior unsecured note of
 fering under 144A/Reg S format\, comprising a 2-year fixed-rate note (IPT:
  T+60a)\, a 2-year floating-rate note (SOFR equivalent)\, and a 5-year fix
 ed-rate note (IPT: T+80a)\, all settling June 9\, 2026\, with expected rat
 ings of Aa1/Stable (Moody's) and AA/Stable (S&P). Proceeds will be used to
  repay $625M of 5.150% Senior Notes due June 2026 and $400M of Floating Ra
 te Senior Notes due May 2027\, with remaining proceeds serving as liquidit
 y resources to effect settlement in the event of a member default. The dea
 l is led by BofA (B&D)\, TD Securities\, and Wells Fargo as active bookrun
 ners.
